From a2d7a6967fc7faf91c93206c0e8d03c3379958aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:41:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 185/193] urltest: modes loss and balance, loss counted from
 the packets of a probe

A URL test cannot see loss. The option mode of a URL test group:

- fastest (the default): as before;
- loss: the delays compared are weighed by the loss of the members, by the
  price of a page measured on the stand (59 + 4.85 RTT + p (155 + 1.2 RTT)
  ms); the member in use and the three best others are probed with 256 KB
  once a loss_interval, and a member the group would switch to without a
  fresh count first with 1 MB; loss every counted member shows is the line's
  and moves nothing;
- balance: connections spread by their source address over at most
  balance_size best members (within the tolerance, loss under
  loss_threshold percent); a device keeps its member, moves at once when it
  is down and after balance_idle without a connection when it left the
  balance (rendezvous hashing).

A loss probe downloads loss_url over a TCP connection of its own with a
receive buffer of 16 KB (common/probesock): the window stays small, so a
shallow queue on the way does not drop a burst of the probe itself. The
headers of its packets are captured from a packet socket with a filter on
its ports, and a hole in the incoming sequence filled later than a quarter
of the RTT counts as a loss, sooner as reordering. A connection that is not
its own (a multiplexed transport, QUIC) is not counted and the member goes
by its delay. The Clash API tells the loss windows (1-24 h), the mode and
the members of a balance.
